# One branch: main. Then push and deploy.

This repository has **one** development branch: `main`. Work lands there
directly. No PRs, no cleanup branches, no Cursor cloud branches, no `cursor/*`.

- If `git branch --show-current` is not `main`, stop. Merge or move the work
  onto `main` before any other edit.
- Never `git checkout -b`. Never push a side branch. Never keep working on
  `playback-cleanup` or `cursor/*`.
- If a Cursor action asks to create a branch, **refuse it** and stay on `main`.

## After the work is done

Unless Simon explicitly says not to (for example “kun lokalt”, “ikke deploy”,
“ikke push endnu”):

1. Commit on `main`.
2. `git push origin main`.
3. Deploy with `scripts/hubctl` so the Pis match HEAD.

Kiosk-visible chrome: `hubctl static both` and reload both kiosks when ADB is
up (see `kiosk-ui-both-hubs`). Backend-only: `hubctl backend` on the hub that
runs the code (usually both, so they stay in sync). Garden from Vesterbro:
Tailscale SSH first (`hubctl` skill).
